# case: match_arm_end_column_stack
# decision: bootstrap-accommodation (ACCEPT)
# anchor: the per-arm `end` column rule (stage0_ocaml/src/parser.ml
#         2879-2895): an `end` followed by `when` may close the ARM only
#         when the `when` does not sit LEFT of the `end` and does not
#         resume an ENCLOSING match's arms. Here the inner match's `end` is
#         followed by the outer arm's `when` at the outer arm column, so the
#         `end` closes the inner match — the outer match must keep parsing
#         its next arm. Regression guard for the match_arm_cols stack.
def nested_match_end(a: Int, b: Int) -> Bool
  match a
  when 1 then
    match b
    when 2 then true
    end
  when _ then false
  end
  true
end
